From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:06:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Drop unused render timestamp records
 by default

Make g16_fs_short and g16_ta_short default to 1 and g16_short_acct to
16. A render without timestamp outputs then gets the fragment sequence
without its two timestamp records and names no TA end timestamp
target, as the macOS driver encodes such a render. Of the stage
timestamps, its receipt then needs only the TA start. About one such
render in 16 of each queue keeps both long forms, and its measured TA
and FS times are credited to the short renders of that queue in the
client's usage and in the statistics. Renders with timestamp outputs
never change.

Measured on the development kernel linux-aurora 1.1107 (experimental),
with the three words set at run time.

One boot, five blocks alternating the words off and on (g16_fs_short 1,
g16_ta_short 1, g16_short_acct 16), off against on as the means of the
blocks, in us per submission:

  render.light depth 1:    162.63 -> 162.40
  render.light depth 8:     54.67 ->  52.95  (-3.1 %)
  render.light depth 64:    54.70 ->  52.67  (-3.7 %)
  compute.light depth 1:   152.57 -> 154.30
  compute.light depth 8:    29.43 ->  29.45
  compute.light depth 64:   19.10 ->  19.00
  fill 1080p:              250.20 -> 250.25
  geometry 1440p:          259.60 -> 262.30

At depth 64 the off blocks read 55.20, 54.35 and 54.55 and the on
blocks 52.60 and 52.75, each the mean of two rows, so every on block is
under both of its neighbours. In the on blocks 94 % of the renders went
out without the records. The pixel check, the readback hash and the
stress pair passed in every block, and no fault line appeared.

On another boot of the same kernel, two clients per setting in the
order off, the two short words, the two with g16_short_acct 16, off
again, render.heavy at depth 64 read 250.22, 250.12, 250.66 and 250.31,
so these words do not change it.

On development kernel 1.1114 (experimental), booted with the three words
0, the six cells of the rows read, in us per submission, one run each,
first with the words 0 and then with them set at run time:

  compute.light depth 1:   154.14 -> 154.44
  compute.light depth 8:    29.93 ->  29.51
  compute.light depth 64:   19.48 ->  19.14
  render.light depth 1:    163.32 -> 162.65
  render.light depth 8:     55.01 ->  53.16  (-3.4 %)
  render.light depth 64:    54.27 ->  52.56  (-3.2 %)

On the same boot with the words on, a compositor frame forced beside a
full render queue passed in 2 of 2 runs, 8 forced frames, with no fault
line and no in-fence line.

On another boot of the same kernel, with the three words on and about
one render in 16 of each queue keeping both long forms, the engine time
a usage monitor reads per render, against the mean of the full records
read before and after on the same boot, two clients each: render.light
vertex -0.6 %, fragment -0.7 %; render.heavy vertex -0.6 %, fragment
0.0 %. Without the accounting word the short renders read no engine time
at all.

g16_fs_short=0 g16_ta_short=0 g16_short_acct=0 at run time restores
the full records.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 24 ++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 5e96058967..d123703261 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -3033,11 +3033,11 @@ pub(crate) fn replay() -> u32 {
     "G16: mask of template pieces (aurora-g16/replay) written into each compute command's sequence record over this driver's values; addresses are never replaced (default 0: none; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_fs_short` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static FS_SHORT: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_fs_short` (runtime 0644, default 1).
+static FS_SHORT: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
 
 /// A render with no timestamp outputs gets the fragment sequence without its two timestamp
-/// records, as the macOS driver encodes such a fragment command.
+/// records, as the macOS driver encodes such a fragment command. Default 1; 0: both records.
 pub(crate) fn fs_short() -> bool {
     FS_SHORT.load(Ordering::Relaxed) != 0
 }
@@ -3048,7 +3048,7 @@ pub(crate) fn fs_short() -> bool {
     FS_SHORT_PARM,
     FS_SHORT,
     "g16_fs_short",
-    "G16: a render without timestamp outputs gets the fragment sequence without its timestamp records (default 0: always both records; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: a render without timestamp outputs gets the fragment sequence without its timestamp records (default 1; 0: always both records; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_resident_units` (0644, default 0; read once, at the latch).
@@ -3294,13 +3294,13 @@ pub(crate) fn lone_ctx_skip() -> bool {
     "G16: 1 = with g16_notifier_cached, retire a render with nothing behind it without the cached record CONTEXT words; stamps, receipts and scene times still prove it (default 1; 0 holds such a render until its cached CONTEXT words are cleaned)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_ta_short` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static TA_SHORT: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_ta_short` (runtime 0644, default 1).
+static TA_SHORT: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
 
 /// `g16_ta_short` 1: a render without timestamp outputs is published with no TA END timestamp
 /// target (TA work +0x8d0 = 0), as macOS's TA pair names none. Its receipt then needs the TA start
 /// and not a TA end after it (stage_stamps.rs); its vertex time is missing from the stage
-/// statistics and the client's usage. Renders with timestamp outputs never change. 0 (default):
+/// statistics and the client's usage. Renders with timestamp outputs never change. Default 1; 0:
 /// no change. Read at each render's publication.
 pub(crate) fn ta_short() -> bool {
     TA_SHORT.load(Ordering::Relaxed) == 1
@@ -3312,18 +3312,18 @@ pub(crate) fn ta_short() -> bool {
     TA_SHORT_PARM,
     TA_SHORT,
     "g16_ta_short",
-    "G16: 1 = renders without timestamp outputs name no TA end timestamp target, as macOS; their receipt needs the TA start only (default 0)"
+    "G16: 1 = renders without timestamp outputs name no TA end timestamp target, as macOS; their receipt needs the TA start only (default 1; 0: the TA end target as before)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_short_acct` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static SHORT_ACCT: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_short_acct` (runtime 0644, default 16).
+static SHORT_ACCT: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(16);
 
 /// `g16_short_acct` = N (2 to 1024; 1 counts as 2), with `g16_fs_short` or `g16_ta_short`: about
 /// one render in N of a queue that would be published short (no timestamp outputs) keeps both
 /// long forms, a jittered interval from N - N/4 to N + N/4, and its measured TA and FS spans
 /// update that queue's moving averages; every short render of the queue is credited those
 /// averages in the client's fdinfo engine time and in the short_acct: statistics line
-/// (short_acct.rs). 0 (default): off, and nothing changes. Read at each render's publication and
+/// (short_acct.rs). Default 16; 0: off, and nothing changes. Read at each render's publication and
 /// retirement.
 pub(crate) fn short_acct() -> u32 {
     match SHORT_ACCT.load(Ordering::Relaxed) {
@@ -3338,7 +3338,7 @@ pub(crate) fn short_acct() -> u32 {
     SHORT_ACCT_PARM,
     SHORT_ACCT,
     "g16_short_acct",
-    "G16: N = one render in about N that g16_fs_short or g16_ta_short would shorten keeps its stamps; short renders are credited its queue's mean stage time (default 0: off; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: N = one render in about N that g16_fs_short or g16_ta_short would shorten keeps its stamps; short renders are credited its queue's mean stage time (default 16; 0: off; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_behind_initbm` (runtime 0644, default 1).
-- 
2.43.0

